{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Infra.Clausen","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Infra.Clausen","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Infra.Polylogarithm"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.Clausen.jonquiereWrongParity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.Clausen.jonquiereWrongParity","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/Clausen.lean#L36-L47","doc":"**Jonquière inversion (closed-form RHS) at depth `n`.**\nThe \"wrong-parity\" part of `Li_n(ζ_K)` equals\n`-(2π i)^n / n! · B_n(1/K)`.\n\nRight now we encode the *real-part* magnitude using a Bernoulli\npolynomial value supplied symbolically (Mathlib has\n`Polynomial.bernoulli` but partial evaluation infrastructure).\nConcrete instances of `JonquiereGeneral` plug in the actual\nBernoulli value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.Clausen.clNAtZetaPredicted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.Clausen.clNAtZetaPredicted","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/Clausen.lean#L26-L34","doc":"Closed form for `Cl_n` at every depth and root of unity index,\npredicted by Theorems E + F + G (the all-depths generalisation\nof Theorems A + B).  For `n` odd this is the orbit-sum\nmultiplier; for `n` even it vanishes (parity case-split). ","signatureChunk":0}]}